# Crystal Imperium play test: the Rare Candy Box and the Pokemon Box Link are in the bag from a
# normal new game (no Nuzlocke), and both work.
# Key Items at new game: 0 RARECANDY BOX, 1 INFIN. REPEL, 2 BOX LINK
!new_game()
!give_mon(155, 5)
expect8 {gPlayerParty+84} 5 cyndaquil_starts_at_level_5

# Rare Candy Box: 999 Rare Candies, usable until the level cap (15 before the first badge). Since
# 0.9.0 the party menu asks how many to use, all 10 up to the cap at first (rare_candy.emu)
!use_key_item(0)
!open_bag_at("POCKET_MEDICINE", 0)
shot 01_rare_candies.png
press A
wait 20
press A
wait 120
press A
wait 60
expect16 {sRareCandyCount} 10 rare_candies_up_to_the_cap
# Use them and keep trying: the cap stops it at 15 (Cyndaquil evolves at 16 since 0.15.0, D44)
mash A 7000
shot 02_stopped_at_cap.png
expect8 {gPlayerParty+84} 15 rare_candies_stop_at_level_cap
mash B 300
wait 60

# Box Link: opens the Pokemon Storage System in the middle of Route 29
!warp(0, 11, 0)
!use_key_item(2)
# use_key_item mashes B, which backs out of the PC menu; open it again and go into the boxes
!open_bag_at("POCKET_KEY_ITEMS", 2)
press A
wait 20
press A
wait 200
press A
wait 200
press A
wait 300
shot 03_box_link_storage.png
expect32 {gMain+4} {CB2_PokeStorage+1} box_link_opens_pokemon_storage
